WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.260
Early morning at a shrine.

2
00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:06.780
Fresh flowers, a candle,
a thin curl of incense.

3
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:09.290
A visitor bows three times.

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.710
Later, she walks clockwise around a stupa.

5
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:17.580
Yet in Theravada teaching, the
Buddha has passed into final peace.

6
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.990
He does not hear or respond.

7
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:24.490
So why bow and give gifts, if
the Buddha cannot receive them?

8
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.250
In this mission, you'll find out
what Buddhists mean by merit,

9
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.010
and why so much depends on giving.

10
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:36.030
Then you'll find out why, for Buddhists,
even merit is not the final goal.

11
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.710
Your mission: explain why
Buddhists bow and give,

12
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.450
even though the Buddha
cannot receive their gifts.
